error":false,"num_turns":40,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I repaired the network by building an estimate of the dead W2 inputs into the first layer. Its dev TTS is 45.0, against 47.9 for the deployed network and 44.8 for the same network with every detector working.\n\n**What I changed and why:** the network relies heavily on the W2 pocket, so with it reading 0 it under-served the W left turn and the queue spilled back into W1u. The first layer is linear before the tanh, so feeding an estimate into the dead inputs reduces to adding to a few existing weight columns. The estimate is:\n- **0.5 × the E2 pocket**, the opposite pocket served by the same phase;\n- **6 × (q_W1u − q_W0u)**, which detects the left pocket spilling back. The difference is essential: a plain q_W1u term caused a gridlock in call 4;\n- **a small 0.15–0.20 prior** outside phase 3, so a lone W2 vehicle isn't stranded once the junction empties.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 370 of the allowed 371.\n\n**Simulator calls:** 6 of 10. Mean dev TTS went 45.9 → 45.3 → 45.1 → gridlock (TTS 151) → 45.1 → 45.0 (final). The last few steps are within noise.\n\n**Final dev TTS:** 45.0 (low 34.9, nominal 45.3, high 54.7). Remaining risk: W2 vehicles can still be stranded if the junction empties while showing phase 2.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 35.1, nominal 45.5, high 55.2.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- weights.npz\n- NOTES.md\n- predictions.json","ttft_ms":1244,"type":"result","duration_ms":865273,"uuid":"442a783e-a669-4fe5-8452-bd2cefa9ebb3","ttft_stream_ms":1049,"time_to_request_ms":36,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":6,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"init_frame_send":1,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":2,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"me